19:T4b8,## The problem: telescoping constructors

When an object has many optional parts, constructors explode:

```
new Burger("wheat", true, false, true, true, false, "bbq");
// …which true is cheese? which is tomato? 🤷
```

You end up with overloaded constructors for every combination, and call sites nobody can read.

## The Builder

Move construction into a separate **builder** object. Each step is a named method that sets one part and **returns the builder itself**, so calls chain fluently. A final `build()` assembles and hands back the finished, usually **immutable**, product:

```
Burger b = new BurgerBuilder()
    .bun("wheat")
    .addPatty()
    .addCheese()
    .build();
```

Now the call site reads like a sentence, optional parts are obvious, and the product can validate itself in `build()` before it ever exists in a half-built state.

## When to use it

- An object with **many optional parameters**.
- You want the product **immutable** (no setters after construction).
- Construction has **steps or invariants** worth enforcing in one place.

> An optional **Director** can encapsulate a common build recipe (e.g. `makeCheeseburger(builder)`) so callers reuse standard configurations.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-creational","activeLesson":"builder"}],["$","$L18","builder",{"lesson":{"id":"builder","patternId":"lld-creational","title":"Builder","kind":"pattern","difficulty":"Core","statement":"Construct a complex object step by step with a readable, chainable API, instead of a monster constructor full of flags.","companies":["Amazon","Google","Uber"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"The telescoping constructor","code":["new Burger(\"wheat\", true, false, true, true, false, \"bbq\");","//          bun   patty cheese ...   which flag is which??"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":1,"narration":"A Burger with many optional parts forces a giant constructor, a wall of positional flags.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"burger","name":"Burger","methods":["+ Burger(bun, patty, cheese,","    lettuce, tomato, sauce)"],"x":0.7,"y":0.4,"tint":"red"}],"relations":[],"shownClassIds":["burger"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["burger"]},"vars":[["call site","unreadable 💥"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":2,"narration":"Is the third argument cheese or tomato? You can't tell. And every new combination needs another overloaded constructor. This doesn't scale.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":[],"shownClassIds":["burger"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["burger"]}}]},{"label":"Build it step by step","code":["Burger b = new BurgerBuilder()","    .bun(\"wheat\")        // each step returns the builder","    .addPatty()","    .addCheese()","    .build();            // assembles the finished Burger"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":1,"narration":"A BurgerBuilder exposes one named method per part. Each setter returns the Builder; build() returns the finished Burger.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"b","name":"BurgerBuilder","methods":["+ bun(b): Builder","+ addPatty(): Builder","+ addCheese(): Builder","+ build(): Burger"],"x":0,"y":0.3,"tint":"accent"},{"id":"p","name":"Burger","fields":["- bun","- patty","- cheese"],"x":2,"y":0.5}],"relations":[{"id":"mk","from":"b","to":"p","kind":"depend","label":"builds"}],"shownClassIds":["b","p"],"shownRelIds":["mk"],"activeIds":["b"]},"vars":[["each setter","returns Builder"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":2,"narration":"The Client starts the chain: bun(\"wheat\").","sequence":{"actors":[{"id":"c","label":"Client","kind":"actor"},{"id":"b","label":"BurgerBuilder","tint":"accent"},{"id":"p","label":"Burger"}],"messages":[{"id":"m1","from":"c","to":"b","label":"bun(\"wheat\")","kind":"call"},{"id":"m2","from":"b","to":"c","label":"this","kind":"return"},{"id":"m3","from":"c","to":"b","label":"addPatty()","kind":"call"},{"id":"m4","from":"c","to":"b","label":"build()","kind":"call"},{"id":"m5","from":"b","to":"p","label":"Burger","kind":"create"},{"id":"m6","from":"b","to":"c","label":"finished burger","kind":"return"}],"shownCount":1,"activeIndex":0}},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":2,"narration":"The builder records the bun and returns ITSELF, that \"return this\" is what lets the next call chain straight on.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:1:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:1:sequence:messages","shownCount":2,"activeIndex":1},"vars":[["returns","this (the builder)"]]},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":3,"narration":"So you keep chaining named steps, addPatty(), addCheese(), …, each one readable and obviously optional.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:1:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:1:sequence:messages","shownCount":3,"activeIndex":2}},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":5,"narration":"Finally build() is called, the one method that assembles everything.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:1:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:1:sequence:messages","shownCount":4,"activeIndex":3}},{"view":"sequence","codeLine":5,"narration":"build() constructs the finished, immutable Burger and returns it. A complex object, assembled by a readable recipe. That's the Builder.","sequence":{"actors":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:1:sequence:actors","messages":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:1:sequence:messages","shownCount":6,"activeIndex":5},"vars":[["result","one immutable Burger ✓"]]}]}]}}]]}]
